!Name: var-exp
!CThese patterns demostrate two closely-related ways of
!Cdoubling the period of rakes whose period is a multiple
!Cof 24. The technique involves an incoming glider that
!Ctoggles the phase of a p24 spaceship. The period-
!Cdoublers can be chained, thus increasing the period
!Cexponentially. These rakes have periods 1536 and 768.
!C
!CDavid Bell, 12 Nov 1999
!
